    <string name="share_text">Get Borsat Dinari to follow dollar and currency prices in Iraq\nhttps://t.me/BorsatDinari</string>
    <string name="language_changed_hint">Choose a language</string>
    <string name="about_updates_title">Latest updates</string>
    <string name="about_updates_text">•  Added 7 new world currencies\n•  Added 10 cryptocurrencies\n•  Added 10 metals\n•  New pages: news, guide, terms of use, help &amp; support, contact channels\n•  Completely redesigned app interface\n•  You can now share the app with your friends</string>
    <string name="guide_home_title">Home page and favorites</string>
    <string name="guide_home_text">•  Home shows 5 favorite markets of your choice; the default is (Baghdad, Erbil official dollar, Basra, Euro).\n•  Drag the three-line handle next to any row to change the order.\n•  The order is saved and stays until you change it.\n•  From the Global or Local market, tap the star next to any item to bring it to Home.\n•  Tap any row to open its price history and choose the period: a day, a week, a month, two months or a custom range from the calendar.\n•  You can export the price history and share it with anyone.\n•  Pull down on any page to refresh the prices, and swipe right or left to move between pages.</string>
    <string name="guide_widget_title">Widgets and their types</string>
    <string name="guide_widget_text">•  Prices widget: shows your first 3 favorites (default: Baghdad, Erbil, Official dollar) with an instant refresh button.\n•  Mini price widget: a small strip showing your first favorite.\n•  Calculator widget: a quick conversion calculator on your home screen.\n•  To add one: long-press an empty spot on your phone\'s home screen, choose “Widgets”, find “Borsat Dinari” and drag the one you want.\n•  Widget order follows the favorites order on Home.</string>
    <string name="guide_colors_title">Price trend explained</string>
    <string name="guide_colors_text">•  Green row with an up triangle: the price rose from the last recorded price.\n•  Red row with a down triangle: the price fell.\n•  Light blue row with no number: the price is stable or no new update is available.\n•  The number next to the triangle (e.g. +500) is the change from the previous price.\n•  The time and date under the price show when this price was actually last updated.</string>
    <string name="guide_update_title">Update period and timing</string>
    <string name="guide_update_text">•  Home: refreshes automatically every 15 minutes while the app is open; you can also refresh manually by pulling down or with the “Refresh prices” tile.\n•  Widgets: refresh automatically about every 15 minutes (Android may delay this to save battery) and have an instant refresh button.\n•  Price history and news: the app keeps the last 60 days.\n•  Price source: the public posts of the Borsat Dinari Telegram channel, so a new price appears when it is posted there.</string>
    <string name="terms_prices_title">Nature of the prices</string>
    <string name="terms_prices_text">The prices shown are taken from public posts (the Borsat Dinari Telegram channel and other public sources) and are for information only. They are not an offer or a commitment to buy or sell at these prices.</string>
    <string name="terms_accuracy_title">No guarantee of accuracy</string>
    <string name="terms_accuracy_text">Prices may differ from real market prices at any moment, and may be delayed, stop updating or contain errors because of the source or the network. Always confirm the actual price with the exchange office or counterparty before any transaction.</string>
    <string name="terms_liability_title">Disclaimer of liability</string>
    <string name="terms_liability_text">The app is provided “as is” without any express or implied warranties. The developer and anyone connected to the app accept no responsibility for any financial or business decision, or for any direct or indirect loss or damage resulting from using the app, relying on its prices, or from outages or errors. Your use of the app and your financial decisions are entirely your own responsibility, and you agree not to claim compensation or bring any claim because of them.</string>
    <string name="terms_advice_title">Not financial advice</string>
    <string name="terms_advice_text">Nothing in the app is financial, investment or legal advice. Consult a professional before making any financial decision.</string>
    <string name="terms_privacy_title">Privacy</string>
    <string name="terms_privacy_text">The app does not request sensitive permissions, collect your personal data or show ads. Your preferences (favorites, language, appearance) are stored only on your device. When you use “Help &amp; support”, your message is sent through the email app you choose.</string>
    <string name="terms_rights_title">Usage rights</string>
    <string name="terms_rights_text">•  There are no copyright or distribution restrictions.\n•  You may use and share the app in any way you like.\n•  The app is open source.</string>
    <string name="terms_changes_title">Changes and acceptance</string>
    <string name="terms_changes_text">These terms may be updated with future versions. By continuing to use the app you accept them.</string>
